    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0932" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg838"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baldwin to Mr. Lee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1896.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 129.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your dispatch
                    No. 169, of the 9th instant, suggesting that a request be made by the minister
                    at Madrid for the amelioration of the condition of Julio Sanguily, esq., during
                    his continued confinement awaiting a new trial, and in reply you are informed
                    that a copy was sent to Mr. Taylor on the 15th instant.</p>
                <p>You are also informed that on the 13th instant a telegram was sent to the
                    minister by the Department in the following words: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In view of Sanguily’s long confinement, now lasting nineteen months, and
                            impairment of his health, you will ask all possible amelioration of his
                            position pending retrial.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0933" n="839" xml:id="pg839"/>
                <p>On the next day a telegram was received from Mr. Taylor stating: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Minister for foreign affairs promises all possible for Sanguily.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Woodward Baldwin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Third Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
